  "notes": "がめつい is a colloquial i-adjective with strong negative connotations. It suggests not just wanting money, but being willing to do unscrupulous things to get it.\n\nSimilar words:\n- {欲|よく}が{深|ふか}い (greedy - more neutral)\n- ケチ (stingy - different nuance, about not spending)\n- {貪欲|どんよく} (avaricious - literary/formal)\n\nThis word is quite direct and insulting if used about someone present.",
